# website/config/template.env
#
# Reference for every VITE_* variable the dashboard build consumes.
#
# Copy to `website/.env` or `website/.env.local` (both gitignored) and fill
# in values for local development. Production injects via CI / the
# orchestrator (Docker build arg, k8s ConfigMap, GitHub Actions env).
#
# Vite makes any variable prefixed with `VITE_` available to the SPA at
# BUILD time. Changing one of these requires a rebuild — the resulting
# bundle is immutable. The only post-build override hatch is the runtime
# `window.__BOT_USERNAME__` global, see `docs/env.md`.

# ── Required for Telegram Login Widget ────────────────────────────────────

# Telegram bot username WITHOUT the leading `@`. The Login Widget uses this
# for the `data-telegram-login` attribute — Telegram refuses to render the
# widget when this is wrong or missing.
#
# Must match the EXACT @username from @BotFather; mismatch leads to
# `INVALID_INIT_DATA` 401s on every login attempt (the server validates the
# HMAC with `CONFIG_BOT_TOKEN`, which is bound to that specific username).
#
# Example: VITE_BOT_USERNAME=vixen_test_bot
VITE_BOT_USERNAME=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the vixen-server REST API. Default `/api/v1` lets Vite proxy
# requests to http://localhost:8000 in dev (configured in vite.config.ts).
#
# For production single-origin deploys keep `/api/v1`. For split deploys
# (dashboard on a CDN, API on a separate host) set an absolute URL —
# e.g. `https://api.vixen.example.com/api/v1`. The server-side
# `CONFIG_CORS_ORIGINS` must allow the dashboard origin in that case.
# VITE_API_URL=/api/v1

# Build metadata. CI injects these from `github.sha` / `github.run_id`
# (see .github/workflows/website-ci.yml). Locally they default to the
# `package.json` version + current ISO time + "unknown". Override only
# when you need a stable string in a debug build.
# VITE_VERSION=
# VITE_BUILD_TIME=
# VITE_GIT_COMMIT=
